lines=['# Fit audit: silent failures across all fitters (TASK-101.7.1)','',f"The audit completed **{len(cases)} scheduled cases, {validation['families']} families and {validation['subsets']} supported held subsets**. It found **{len(failures)} strict-target silent-failure cases** ({unique_failures} distinct input/hold witnesses) across **{len({r['family'] for r in failures})} families**. {counts(refs)}. Case counts are stress-grid hits, not prevalence estimates or counts of independent defects.",'', '## Findings that warrant fixes','', 'The clearest objective failures include:','', '- **Held-scale beta-prime:** direct log-beta/likelihood subtraction gives large errors on nearly constant data. Case 248 reports logLik 80 instead of 84.441950547…; case 249 reports about -5.05e10 instead of 130.493688857…. The relevant calculation is `betapr/mle.hpp:130–131`, calling `special/special.hpp:83–87`.', '- **Held-shape NSBeta:** nearby digamma subtraction falsely brackets a shape root; lgamma subtraction also corrupts logLik. The held path in `nsbeta/mle.hpp:23–25` bypasses the repaired beta path and does not forward iterlim to its inner helper.', '- **Transformed gamma families:** `invgamma/mle.hpp:49–53`, `lgamma/mle.hpp:23–28`, and `naka/mle.hpp:45–55` round reciprocal/log/squared observations before delegating. Nearly constant raw observations lose information before the stable gamma solver receives them.', '- **Held Burr shape:** `burr/mle.hpp:310,344,351` amplifies rounded log differences at large power. The returned-point likelihood and high-precision stationary point disagree on tightly clustered data.','']
if focused:lines.extend([f"For the NSBeta witness (case {focused['case']}), shape2 is returned as **{short(focused['returned_shape2'],12)}**, while the unique held-shape reference is **{short(focused['reference_shape2'],12)}**. The reference MLE logLik is **{short(focused['reference_logLik_at_MLE'],16)}**, versus reported **{focused['returned_reported_logLik']}**. Its bracket was computed at 350 digits and its signs retained at 700 digits. Strict concavity in the free shape establishes uniqueness; the sign evaluations remain numerical. See [the focused reference](2026-11-07-fit-audit-data/focused-reference.json).",''])
lines.extend(['The coefficient-only category is deliberately separate: it violates the brief’s 1e-8 coefficient target even when likelihood loss is tiny and the fitter’s documented default tolerance is looser. Those rows are not evidence of a beta-prime-sized objective error. Their local information and stationarity checks are recorded. The final residual/information check also requires a linearized relative root-error proxy below 1e-10 and below one hundredth of the measured coefficient displacement; this is a numerical local consistency check, not a rigorous curvature enclosure (`root-precision-check.json`).','', '## Method','', 'The standalone C++17 harness reuses `dev/validation/diagnostics.py` and the shared binding call routes. It observes the core result before binding error conversion, retains 17 digits of each returned double, and preserves default controls and golden held values. All declared structural `holds:` exclusions are omitted exactly as in that sweep. The checkout has 99 golden-backed fitters, including `st`, rather than the 98 in the brief. No fitter, golden, dossier, binding or production test was changed.','', 'The audit-local generator adapts diagnostic error callbacks to the current structured-error interface and repairs the GB2 observer coefficient mapping. These changes are confined to the generated audit harness; the shared fitter routes, their default controls and production sources are unchanged.', '', 'Samples include 12-observation interior subsets; n = 2, 3, 5; heavy ties; nearly constant samples at distinct valid locations with relative spread 1e-4, 1e-8, 1e-12; endpoint distances 1e-6, 1e-12, 1e-17, 1e-200 where representable; exact interior ULP complements; scales 1e-150 and 1e150; location offsets 1e8; concentration/outlier probes; and large, nearly constant and zero-but-one counts. Conditional support expressions are evaluated from metadata. The initial generic fallback for parameters named min/max was found insufficient; `support_samples.py` adds the missing endpoint and valid-location cases. Incompatible held-support samples remain as explicit rejection controls.','',f'There are also {len(recipes)} finite parameter sequences toward named faces in {len({r["family"] for r in recipes})} families (K = 100 and 1e6 where representable). SciPy quantiles generate data only. Coupled-quantile convolution sequences are labelled as data sequences, not exact convolution quantiles. The exact binary64 `cases.json` is frozen for replay. Held values are the golden values; this does not exhaust the continuum of possible held values.','', 'The reference parser is `quality/density.py`, explicitly using README `log_density` rather than golden-specific `spec.py`. Inputs and returned doubles are converted exactly to mpmath. Working precision is at least 70 digits and escalates with magnitude; stable log1p rewrites, interval masses, centered CMP sums with geometric tail bounds, Hurwitz-zeta identities, atomic members and the implicit Tukey density are in `reference_extra.py`. Strict support exclusions are proved separately with exact rational representations of binary64 inputs and coefficients (`support_geometry.py`); equality at endpoints is not classified by that check. Such witnesses have exact zero likelihood at the returned point, even when the gap is only one ULP. They call for feasibility projection, not a claim that a conditional exact-arithmetic certificate has been disproved. Silent finite likelihood/improvement witnesses are checked again at doubled precision. This is numerical evidence, not an outward-rounded error enclosure.','', 'The logLik threshold is 1e-8 × max(1, |reported logLik|). The search evaluates scaled free-coordinate scores, feasible coordinate moves, adjacent integer moves, a feasible golden seed, location/data-extreme probes, and up to twelve high-precision Newton iterations. Score findings require magnitude above 1e-3 and a feasible ascent witness. A coefficient-only finding requires error above 1e-8, a better point, per-observation stationarity residual below 1e-18, and positive local information with minimum eigenvalue above 1e-35 × max(1, maximum eigenvalue). Positive parameters use ordinary relative error; signed coordinates use max(1, |reference|) in the denominator. For narrow truncated-normal windows, the mean-coordinate probe uses sd²/window width, the natural tilt scale; ordinary data-scale probes can miss a large score. Nonsmooth/bound/integer coordinates are not treated as smooth root coordinates. Tukey-lambda uses 260 inversion bisections; its implicit derivatives are not used.','', 'The initial core wall guard is three seconds, followed by twenty-second retries. Initial reference guards are two seconds, with targeted retries at 10–20 seconds. These are audit guards, not changes to iterlim. A wall-guarded call has no observed native terminal status and remains open. Finite-MLE claims for stopped fits use the sufficient conditions in `existence.py`, including dossier results, fixed-shape coercivity/tie conditions, or finite likelihood at the sole fully held point. The truncated-normal criterion in `tnorm_existence.py` uses strict concavity of the quadratic exponential family and compares its empirical sufficient statistic with the exponential/uniform boundary; high-precision signs carry a stated margin. Nonexistence/incompatible support proofs are recorded separately. A finite start or a local maximum alone is never used to prove global attainment.','', 'The audit targets core statuses. For example, the Weibull, inverse-Weibull and Gumbel binding routes reject nonfinite logLik, so some nonfinite core-Ok findings are caught before an R/JS result is returned. The GED route checks coefficients but not logLik at that check. Binding-wide propagation beyond these inspected routes is not a claim of this audit.','', '## Per-family summary','',legend,'', '| Family | Cases | Silent | Loud | ok / proved stop | Numerical open | Existence open | Worst E |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|'])
