lines.extend(['','## Static scan','',f"The recursive scan covers fitter headers and included helpers (excluding dpqr.hpp), with {len(static)} nominations: {dict(collections.Counter(h['kind'] for h in static))}. [The full file:line inventory](2026-11-07-fit-audit-data/static-inventory.md) gives each matched line, contextual review and dynamic family-level evidence.",'', 'Important distinctions: the one-pass log variance at `kumar/mle.hpp:151` is cancellation-prone, but fallback/certificate paths can protect it; its mere presence is not a demonstrated public-fit defect. `core/newton.hpp:12,36–40,59` records legacy parity and step-only termination, requiring caller-specific score/bracket review. The fixed hundred-step bisection at `ztpois/mle.hpp:17–22` has no convergence/exhaustion gate; no harmful case was established here. Small fixed matrix loops are not numerical iteration caps. `nbinom/mle.hpp:168` and `zip/mle.hpp:136` contain direct log complements, but execution paths and later gates matter.','', 'The demonstrated held-scale beta-prime path reaches the direct lgamma difference in `special::lbeta`. A future stable shared log-beta change would also require checking its density callers. This audit did not change or audit settled dpqr/truth/codegen outputs.','', '## Ranked fix list','', 'All silent categories precede loud failures. Within that ordering, finite wrong likelihoods / meaningful ascent on plausible samples rank above strict coefficient-accuracy misses and nonfinite payloads on extreme scales; breadth of held subsets and sample classes breaks ties. Frequency in this constructed grid is not real-data prevalence. Cause descriptions outside the specifically traced paths remain hypotheses.','', '| Rank | Family | Silent / loud cases | Held subsets affected | Exposure | Worst E | Fix direction / source |','|---|---|---|---:|---|---:|---|'])
def priority(item):
 f,rr=item;bad=[r for r in rr if r['classification'] in ['silent failure','loud failure']];silent=[r for r in bad if r['classification']=='silent failure']
